; Generated by c64-source. Edit the values here: generate keeps them.
; The switches of the build. Each switch is 0 or 1: change a value, then build again.
; The defaults give the clean program: copy protection, trainers, cheats and
; changes of a crack are 0, and the fixes of the releases are 1.
; generate adds a new switch with its default and removes a switch that the
; knowledge does not have. The build of a release does not read this file.

; Copy protection: off by default
PROTECTION_LOADER_CHECK = 0 ; on in ANON, BANDIT, DR. $43ae-$43b0. F3 during play sets fkey_code 2. The main loop then wants 4 in $0342, a value of the original loading (the Bandit dump of a running game has it). Any other value starts the rank screen: the game ends. ANON ($c8) and BANDIT ($00) fail the check, DR (4) passes.
PROTECTION_TABLE        = 0 ; on in BANDIT, DR. $5eea-$5eec. The original loader leaves an identity table (00..ff) at $d100, in the RAM under the I/O area. The game copies it to $1000 at $5ed8 and reads it there. The anonymous crack (base) puts the table at $1000 itself and writes NOP over the store at $5eea.

; Trainers: off by default
TRAINER_BOMBS           = 0 ; on in DR. $63f0-$63f2. Derbyshire Ram trainer "BOMBS CHEAT?": LDA in place of DEC of the bomb counter.
TRAINER_FUEL            = 0 ; on in DR. $4605-$4607. Derbyshire Ram trainer "FUEL CHEAT?": LDA in place of DEC of the fuel counter.

; Cheats: off by default
CHEAT_INVINCIBLE        = 0 ; on in no release. $5d46-$5d47. read_keys has a disabled key toggle of the invincible flag ($4080): LDA #$78 / BNE always skips it. The patch puts AND #$78 there, so holding F1, F3, F5 and F7 together toggles invincibility. No release has this byte: the patch is a reconstruction.

; Changes of a crack: off by default
CRACK_DR_BOOT           = 0 ; on in DR. $8000-$804c. Derbyshire Ram boot code with a CBM80 header at $8000, in the map buffer: builds the $d100 table, the $0200 routine and the loader values at $1100/$1130/$1142, jumps to $8100, which copies $1100-$11ff to $0300 and jumps to $4000. The map rows of play write over it.

; Other changes
EDITION_SYNSOFT         = 0 ; on in DR. $7364-$7382. The title line of the DR release reads "COPYRIGHT 1983 SYNSOFT" (centred) in place of "COPYRIGHT 1983 SYNAPSE SOFTWARE". No other game byte differs for this.
RUN_STATE_BANDIT        = 0 ; on in BANDIT. $3c50-$3c57, $3ca0-$3caf, $4006-$407b, $4085-$40f1, $4788-$4808, $483c-$483d, $8000-$804c. Values that a game that ran left in the image of the Bandit memory dump: variables, self-modified operands of the scroll code and the map buffer at $8000.
RUN_STATE_DR            = 0 ; on in DR. $4006-$407b, $4085-$40f1. Values that a game that ran left in the image of the Derbyshire Ram release: variables and self-modified operands.

; Leftovers: off by default
LEFTOVERS = 0 ; 348 bytes in 6 files in leftovers/ that nothing uses. 1 builds them, so main.asm gives the bytes of the program. Each release has them. The loader never loads them
